+- **Wide open there are no rays at all, because there is no polygon.** The blades retract into
+  the round barrel, and at `Maximum Aperture` they are flush with it: the pupil is the barrel's
+  circle, and a circle diffracts into rings. The iris polygon only emerges from the barrel as
+  you stop down (below `p = N_open/N ≈ cos(pi/n)` it is clear of it entirely), and the rays come
+  out with it. That is the other half of "sunstars appear when you stop down".
 - **Blade Curvature shortens and softens the rays** — a rounded outline has less straight edge
